# Project Rules for Cursor 2.0 - QA Evidence Center

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 15 App Router + TypeScript strict mode
- **Code Quality**: ESLint + Prettier (configured)
- **ORM**: Prisma (MySQL 8.0)
- **Validation**: Zod schemas for all inputs
- **Auth**: NextAuth.js (Credentials provider first, Google OAuth optional)
- **UI**: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui components
- **Icons**: lucide-react
- **State Management**: Zustand
- **Data Fetching**: TanStack Query (React Query)
- **Charts**: recharts
- **PDF**: puppeteer or @react-pdf/renderer (future)

## Database & ORM Rules
- Use Prisma ORM with MySQL 8.0
- Generate typesafe code with Zod on all inputs
- Use `BigInt` for IDs (Prisma default)
- Use `upsert` for idempotent operations in seeds
- Never store binary files in DB - EvidenceFile stores metadata only (storage_type, path, drive_id, url)

## Authentication & Authorization
- NextAuth.js with Credentials provider (primary)
- Google OAuth optional (for future)
- RBAC implementation from `Role.code` (ADMIN, QA_LEAD, TEACHER, ASSESSOR)
- School scoping via `UserSchoolRole` - users can only access data from schools they're assigned to
- Middleware for route protection and RBAC checks

## Evidence Code Generation
- Format: `${indicator.code}-${running2digits}` (e.g., 2.3-01, 2.3-02)
- Generated within same fiscal_year
- Use `nextEvidenceCode(indicatorId, fiscalYear)` helper function
- Fiscal year calculation: Oct-Dec = year + 544, Jan-Sep = year + 543

## Data Seeding
- Build idempotent seeds for:
  - Roles (ADMIN, QA_LEAD, TEACHER, ASSESSOR)
  - EduLevels (EARLY_CHILDHOOD, BASIC)
  - QAStandards, QAIndicators, QASubIndicators (both EC and BASIC)
  - Demo school and admin user
- Use `upsert` or check existence before insert
- Support `npm run db:reset` command

## UI/UX Rules
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Use shadcn/ui components (install via CLI)
- Use lucide-react for icons
- Follow WCAG AA accessibility guidelines
- Use semantic HTML
- Responsive design (mobile-first)
- Primary font: Kanit (for Thai text)
- i18n ready (primary language: Thai)

## State & Data Management
- Use Zustand for client-side state
- Use TanStack Query for server state and data fetching
- Use Server Actions for form submissions (Next.js 15)
- Use React Hook Form + Zod for form validation

## File Storage
- **DO NOT** store binary files in database
- EvidenceFile model stores:
  - `storageType`: LOCAL | GDRIVE | URL
  - `storagePath`: path for local files
  - `driveFileId`: Google Drive file ID
  - `externalUrl`: external URL
- When setting primary file, reset other files in same evidence

## Testing
- Write unit tests for helper functions (e.g., `thaiFiscalYear()`, `nextEvidenceCode()`)
- Use Jest or Vitest for unit tests
- Use Playwright for E2E tests (smoke tests)
- Minimum coverage: 70% for helpers

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode enabled
- ESLint configured and must pass (no errors, no warnings)
- Prettier formatted
- Use async/await (no callbacks)
- Use const/let (no var)
- Prefer named exports
- Use meaningful variable names (Thai comments OK, but code in English)

## API Routes
- Use Next.js App Router API routes (`/app/api/*`)
- Use Server Actions for form submissions
- Validate all inputs with Zod
- Check RBAC and school scoping in every route
- Log critical actions to AuditLog

## Audit Logging
- Log important events:
  - CREATE_EVIDENCE
  - UPDATE_EVIDENCE_STATUS
  - UPLOAD_FILE
  - CREATE_REVIEW
  - LOGIN
  - LOGOUT
- Store in AuditLog table with actor, action, target, payload

## Performance
- Lighthouse score target: ≥ 85
- Use Next.js Image component for images
- Optimize database queries (use indexes)
- Use pagination for large lists

## Security
- Never expose sensitive data in client-side code
- Hash passwords with bcrypt
- Validate all inputs server-side
- Use CSRF protection (NextAuth handles this)
- Sanitize user inputs

## Error Handling
- Use try-catch for async operations
- Return proper HTTP status codes
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Log errors server-side

## Documentation
- Comment complex logic
- Use JSDoc for functions
- Keep README.md updated
- Document API routes
